Subject: [oss-security] CVE-2022-34169: Apache Xalan Java XSLT library is vulnerable to an
 integer truncation issue when processing malicious XSLT stylesheets 

Description:

The Apache Xalan Java XSLT library is vulnerable to an integer truncation i=
ssue when processing malicious XSLT stylesheets. This can be used to corrup=
t Java class files generated by the internal XSLTC compiler and execute arb=
itrary Java bytecode.

The Apache Xalan Java project is dormant and in the process of being retire=
d. No future releases of Apache Xalan Java to address this issue are expect=
ed.

Note: Java runtimes (such as OpenJDK) include repackaged copies of Xalan.

